### item 9 ADR
7:## Context
9:The repository tracked `resources/tools/genetics/genetic_risk_predictor.pkl`, a scikit-learn model saved with `pickle`. Two scripts came with it:
11:- `resources/tools/genetics/train_dummy_model.py` trained a `RandomForestClassifier` on `make_classification` random data and pickled it.
12:- `resources/tools/genetics/genetic_predictor.py` loaded the pickle at import time and presented its output as a "probability of carrying a pathogenic variant".
18:## Decision
20:1. Delete the three files: `genetic_risk_predictor.pkl`, `genetic_predictor.py` and `train_dummy_model.py`.
21:2. Adopt the rule: **no pickle or other code-executing serialization artifact is tracked in the repository or shipped in the package.** This covers `pickle`, `joblib`, `dill`, `cloudpickle`, `shelve`, PyTorch checkpoints loaded with `torch.load`, and NumPy files loaded with `allow_pickle=True`.
24:   - `.gitignore` ignores `*.pkl`, `*.pickle` and `*.joblib`.
