### item 12 PR draft
6:## What it does
8:- Stops tracking `.devcontainer/.env` and adds `.devcontainer/.env.example` with variable names only (`GOOGLE_API_KEY`, `PYTHONPATH`, `GFL_ENV`).
11:- Adds secret scanning at two layers with the same rules (`.gitleaks.toml`, gitleaks upstream defaults):
13:  - workflow `.github/workflows/secret-scan.yml` (job `gitleaks`) on pull requests and pushes to `main`. It scans the commit range and the tree, and fails on any finding.
16:## Why
18:- `.devcontainer/.env` was public. Its credentials must be treated as leaked: the owner rotates them (list of services kept privately by the maintainers). This PR stops further exposure; it does not rewrite history.
21:- On pull requests the scan loads `.gitleaks.toml` from the base commit, so a PR cannot widen its own allowlist.
24:## How to reproduce
28:git archive HEAD | tar -x -C /tmp/gfl-head && gitleaks dir /tmp/gfl-head --config .gitleaks.toml --redact   # no leaks found
33:## Impact on results
39:- `.devcontainer/.env`: removed from the index. The file was not opened.
40:- `.github/workflows/secret-scan.yml`: new workflow.
41:- `.gitleaks.toml`: scan configuration. Widening it weakens the guard.
42:- `.pre-commit-config.yaml`: one hook block appended.
